---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Legal
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How Stockpile collects, uses, and protects your information, and which third-party services (Privy, Jupiter, Helius and others) are involved."
	updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
>
	<p class="lead">
		Stockpile is a non-custodial app that turns news stories into bags of tokenized stocks and pre-IPO tokens on Solana. This
		Privacy Policy explains what information we collect when you use the Stockpile mobile app and website (the "Service"), how we
		use it, and who we share it with.
	</p>
	<div class="callout">
		<strong>The short version:</strong> we never have your private keys or recovery phrase. We store your email, your public
		wallet address, the bags you save, and the swaps you attribute to bags. We use no advertising or analytics trackers, and we
		never sell your data. Anything you do on the Solana blockchain is public by design.
	</div>

	<h2 id="collect">1. Information we collect</h2>
	<h3>Information you provide</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Sign-in details.</strong> The email address you sign in with. Sign-in and one-time codes are handled by Privy.</li>
		<li><strong>Profile.</strong> An optional username and display name.</li>
		<li><strong>Saved bags.</strong> The bags you bookmark.</li>
		<li><strong>Support messages.</strong> Anything you send us when you contact support or give feedback.</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Information created when you use the Service</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Wallet address.</strong> The public address of the embedded Solana wallet Privy creates for you, together with your Privy
			user ID.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Trade requests.</strong> When you ask for a quote or build a swap, we receive the tokens, amounts, and wallet address
			involved so we can fetch quotes from Jupiter and prepare the transactions.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Signed transactions.</strong> Transactions you sign on your device are sent to our API, which relays them to the Solana
			network through Helius and tracks whether they confirm.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Bag positions.</strong> For each confirmed swap you attribute to a bag, we store the transaction signature, token,
			direction, amounts, and block time. We read these from the blockchain, not from your device, and use them to show your cost
			basis and performance per bag.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Portfolio and activity.</strong> We read your wallet's public balances and transaction history from the blockchain so we
			can show them in the app. We fetch these when you ask for them and do not keep a separate copy beyond the bag positions above.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Collected automatically</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Technical data.</strong> When your device talks to our servers, our hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes your IP
			address, request metadata, and basic device and app-version information as part of normal operation and security.
		</li>
		<li><strong>App updates.</strong> The app checks Expo's update service for new versions, which shares your app version and platform.</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>What we do not collect</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Private keys and recovery phrases.</strong> Your embedded wallet's keys are secured by Privy's key-management system and
			are never available to Stockpile. We cannot move your funds and cannot recover your wallet.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Advertising or analytics trackers.</strong> The app has no third-party analytics, advertising, or cross-app tracking SDKs.</li>
		<li><strong>Device data.</strong> We do not access your contacts, photos, camera, microphone, or precise location.</li>
		<li><strong>Bank or card details.</strong> Stockpile does not process fiat payments.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="blockchain">2. Public blockchain data</h2>
	<p>
		Solana is a public blockchain. Your wallet address, balances, and every transaction you make are permanently and publicly
		visible to anyone, and can be linked to you if your address is ever associated with your identity. Stockpile cannot change,
		hide, or delete information recorded on-chain.
	</p>

	<h2 id="use">3. How we use your information</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>To create and secure your account and embedded wallet.</li>
		<li>To show your saved bags, portfolio, activity, and per-bag performance.</li>
		<li>To get swap quotes, prepare transactions, sponsor network fees, and relay your signed transactions to Solana.</li>
		<li>To enforce eligibility and restrictions, and to detect and prevent fraud, abuse, and security incidents.</li>
		<li>To operate, debug, and improve the Service.</li>
		<li>To reply to support requests and send important service or policy notices.</li>
		<li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>We do not use your information for advertising, and we do not sell or rent it.</p>

	<h2 id="third-parties">4. Third-party services</h2>
	<p>Stockpile relies on these providers. Each has its own privacy policy and terms.</p>
	<h3>Providers that process data about you</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong><a href="https://www.privy.io/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privy</a></strong>: sign-in,
			email one-time codes, and embedded wallet infrastructure. Privy processes your email, device and session details, and wallet
			keys under its own security model.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong><a href="https://jup.ag/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Jupiter</a></strong>: token swap
			aggregation and routing across Solana liquidity, plus token metadata and prices. Jupiter receives the wallet address, tokens,
			and amounts involved in each quote and swap.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong><a href="https://www.helius.dev/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Helius</a></strong>: Solana RPC
			infrastructure. We use it to read balances and transaction history, simulate transactions, and send your signed transactions to
			the network.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</a></strong>:
			hosting for our API and website, content delivery, and security. It also connects our API to our managed Postgres database.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong><a href="https://expo.dev/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Expo</a></strong>: delivers over-the-air app
			updates.
		</li>
		<li><strong>Apple App Store and Google Play</strong>: app distribution, under their own policies.</li>
	</ul>
	<h3>Data and content providers (no personal data sent by us)</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Backed Finance (<a href="https://xstocks.fi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">xStocks</a>)</strong> and
			<strong><a href="https://prestocks.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PreStocks</a></strong>: token issuers whose
			product metadata and logos we display.
		</li>
		<li><strong>tokens.xyz</strong>: price chart data.</li>
		<li><strong>Pyth Network</strong>: reference prices for the underlying assets.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>CongressInvests</strong> and the official U.S. House and Senate disclosure sites: public STOCK Act trading disclosures
			used to build disclosure bags.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>OpenAI</strong>: helps us curate and summarize public news stories on our servers. None of your personal data is sent to
			OpenAI.
		</li>
		<li><strong>DiceBear</strong>: generates default profile avatars from a seed value.</li>
		<li>
			<strong>News publishers</strong>: the stories we link to belong to their publishers. When you tap "Read story", the publisher's
			site opens and its own privacy policy applies.
		</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		Some images, such as token logos, news images, and avatars, load directly from these providers' servers. Like any web request,
		this exposes your IP address to the host.
	</p>

	<h2 id="sharing">5. How we share information</h2>
	<p>We share information only:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>with the service providers above, as needed to run the Service;</li>
		<li>when required by law, regulation, subpoena, or other legal process;</li>
		<li>to protect the rights, property, or safety of Stockpile, our users, or others, including to investigate fraud or sanctions violations;</li>
		<li>as part of a merger, acquisition, financing, or sale of assets, subject to this Policy; or</li>
		<li>with your consent.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="retention">6. Data retention</h2>
	<p>
		We keep account data (email, username, wallet address, saved bags, and bag positions) for as long as your account is active.
		When you delete your account, we delete this data within 30 days, except where we must keep it to meet legal obligations,
		resolve disputes, or enforce our agreements. Server logs are kept for a short period for security and debugging. Data held by
		Privy and other providers follows their own retention policies. On-chain data cannot be deleted.
	</p>
	<p>Some data, such as cached bags and preferences, is stored on your device and is removed when you sign out or delete the app.</p>

	<h2 id="security">7. Security</h2>
	<p>
		All traffic between the app and our servers is encrypted with TLS. Access to our database and secrets is restricted, and the
		transactions we prepare are checked and simulated before you are asked to sign them. No system is perfectly secure, however,
		and you are responsible for keeping your device and your sign-in email secure.
	</p>

	<h2 id="rights">8. Your rights and choices</h2>
	<p>Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, UK GDPR, or CCPA/CPRA), you may have the right to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>access the personal data we hold about you and receive a portable copy;</li>
		<li>correct inaccurate data;</li>
		<li>delete your account and personal data;</li>
		<li>object to or restrict certain processing; and</li>
		<li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> from the address linked to your
		account. We will respond within the time required by law. We do not sell or "share" personal information for cross-context
		behavioral advertising as those terms are defined under California law. You may also complain to your local data protection
		authority.
	</p>
	<p>
		Deleting your Stockpile account does not delete your wallet or its funds. Before you delete your account, move your assets or
		export your wallet through Privy.
	</p>

	<h2 id="children">9. Children</h2>
	<p>
		Stockpile is not intended for anyone under 18. We do not knowingly collect information from minors. If we learn that we have, we
		will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2 id="international">10. International transfers</h2>
	<p>
		We and our providers operate in the United States and other countries. Your information may be processed outside your country,
		under data protection laws that may differ from yours. Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as standard
		contractual clauses.
	</p>

	<h2 id="changes">11. Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we will notify you in the app or on this page before
		they take effect. The "Last updated" date shows the latest version.
	</p>

	<h2 id="contact">12. Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Questions about this Policy or our data practices? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
	</p>
</Legal>
